From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:41:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-glymur: Keep the USB4 router 0 domains on for
 an awake path

When a USB4 host router keeps a connected partner across system sleep,
the router and its PHY are on the awake path, but genpd still powers
off GCC_USB4_0_GDSC and GCC_USB_0_PHY_GDSC during system suspend and
drops their votes on the parent CX domain. The router GDSC then loses
the router state, CX can collapse under the PHY, and the link cannot be
resumed.

Set GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP on the two domains, so that genpd leaves
them, and their parent, on while a device in them is on the awake path.
Without such a device the domains are switched off as before. Only
router 0 is handled; the domains of routers 1 and 2 are unchanged.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
index 07242a98a41..84fc47f507f 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
@@ -7733,6 +7733,8 @@ static struct gdsc gcc_usb4_0_gdsc = {
 	.clk_dis_wait_val = 0xf,
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "gcc_usb4_0_gdsc",
+		/* A router kept across system sleep holds its state here. */
+		.flags = GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP,
 	},
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
@@ -7769,6 +7771,8 @@ static struct gdsc gcc_usb_0_phy_gdsc = {
 	.clk_dis_wait_val = 0x2,
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "gcc_usb_0_phy_gdsc",
+		/* The PHY of a router kept across system sleep stays initialized. */
+		.flags = GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP,
 	},
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
-- 
2.56.0

